      "content": "thanks. so u said for Case B that the environment acts as an aggravating factor because it's linked to a \"more difficult or unremorseful lifestyle\"... that sounds a bit vague. \n\ncan u be more specific? like, if a judge is looking at the \"risk to society\" or \"likelihood of re-offending,\" would someone from an underserved urban area naturally be seen as a higher risk compared to the guy in Case A? basically, how much does the actual neighborhood or socioeconomic status weigh into the actual decision for jail vs probation?",
